00:31:44.450 --> 00:31:47.420
teams to stay connected
outside of meetings

00:31:47.420 --> 00:31:52.440
to foster well-being and
reduce video call fatigue.

00:31:52.440 --> 00:31:55.230
We made communication
and collaboration

00:31:55.230 --> 00:31:56.970
completely seamless.

00:31:56.970 --> 00:32:00.810
For instance, users can
easily present and collaborate

00:32:00.810 --> 00:32:04.290
in meetings, create meeting
notes from their calendar,

00:32:04.290 --> 00:32:07.980
present and meet directly
from doc sheets of slides,

00:32:07.980 --> 00:32:11.670
and collaborate directly
from chat and spaces.

00:32:11.670 --> 00:32:15.810
We optimize collaboration
from all mobile devices

00:32:15.810 --> 00:32:20.970
to provide great experiences for
frontline workers who make up

00:32:20.970 --> 00:32:24.120
80% of the global workforce.

00:32:24.120 --> 00:32:27.540
One of America's largest
hospital systems,

00:32:27.540 --> 00:32:30.930
CommonSpirit Health, is
advancing its mission

00:32:30.930 --> 00:32:34.170
during the pandemic by
making its frontline doctors

00:32:34.170 --> 00:32:37.860
and nurses productive
at Google Workspace.

00:32:37.860 --> 00:32:40.590
Since hybrid work has
removed the notion

00:32:40.590 --> 00:32:44.280
for physical location for
work, Google Workspace

00:32:44.280 --> 00:32:49.950
created Spaces, a unified,
digital location for work.

00:32:49.950 --> 00:32:53.220
Today, more than
three billion users

00:32:53.220 --> 00:32:58.180
move securely and seamlessly
between Mail, Chat, Audio,

00:32:58.180 --> 00:33:00.750
Video, and now, Spaces.

00:33:00.750 --> 00:33:06.840
And you, too, can choose among
the over 5,300 public apps

00:33:06.840 --> 00:33:09.210
in our marketplace,
and you can also

00:33:09.210 --> 00:33:15.060
add thousands of private apps
to enhance your workspace.

00:33:15.060 --> 00:33:17.700
And I want to step
aside for just a minute

00:33:17.700 --> 00:33:21.430
and tell you about a hidden
secret in our portfolio

00:33:21.430 --> 00:33:26.160
of products, AppSheet,
our no code platform that

00:33:26.160 --> 00:33:31.050
makes it easy for everyone, not
just professional developers

00:33:31.050 --> 00:33:34.440
to build amazing
apps and workflows.

00:33:34.440 --> 00:33:38.340
For instance, property
managers at car Ford properties

00:33:38.340 --> 00:33:41.520
use the AppSheet to
build a mobile app

00:33:41.520 --> 00:33:45.000
to log, track, and resolve
problems with headquarters,

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:48.880
replacing a multi-step
manual process.

00:33:48.880 --> 00:33:51.210
We're also partnering
with Citrix,

00:33:51.210 --> 00:33:55.710
because employees sometimes need
access to Windows and Mac OS

00:33:55.710 --> 00:34:00.300
applications and desktops
directly served from the Cloud.

00:34:00.300 --> 00:34:02.400
We're expanding our
partnership with Citrix

00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:07.020
today to deliver an integrated
desktop as a service solution

00:34:07.020 --> 00:34:11.630
purpose built on Google Cloud.

00:34:11.630 --> 00:34:16.520
Now, customers ask us, do we
know that our data systems

00:34:16.520 --> 00:34:19.610
and users are
secure, and how do we

00:34:19.610 --> 00:34:23.110
keep them secure in the future?

00:34:23.110 --> 00:34:28.210
As more digital users access
more data from more locations,

00:34:28.210 --> 00:34:32.949
the risk of cybersecurity
breaches is accelerating.

00:34:32.949 --> 00:34:36.280
By pioneering new
approaches to security,

00:34:36.280 --> 00:34:39.219
Google keeps more
people safe online

00:34:39.219 --> 00:34:42.610
than anyone else in the world.

00:34:42.610 --> 00:34:44.620
Take, for instance, JetBlue.

00:34:44.620 --> 00:34:47.949
It's keeping its system
secure, protecting

00:34:47.949 --> 00:34:52.090
the data of all its travelers,
and modernizing its security

00:34:52.090 --> 00:34:55.840
operations using Chronicle
to detect threats

00:34:55.840 --> 00:34:58.930
across petabytes of
security telemetry

00:34:58.930 --> 00:35:03.030
and eliminating
data blind spots.

00:35:03.030 --> 00:35:06.690
Commerzbank, one of
Germany's largest banks

00:35:06.690 --> 00:35:09.990
is using a new certificate
authority service

00:35:09.990 --> 00:35:13.800
to verify machine and
workload identity,

00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:18.270
improving security, simplifying
operations, eliminating

00:35:18.270 --> 00:35:20.490
entire classes of threats.

00:35:20.490 --> 00:35:23.400
Secure by default
drives customers

00:35:23.400 --> 00:35:24.990
to choose Google Cloud.

00:35:24.990 --> 00:35:27.750
First, we've
implemented zero trust

00:35:27.750 --> 00:35:30.780
at the core of our services
and our operations,

00:35:30.780 --> 00:35:33.570
enabling you to trust nothing.

00:35:33.570 --> 00:35:38.110
Second, we've built Cloud scale
threat detection and response,

00:35:38.110 --> 00:35:40.590
allowing you to
detect everything.

00:35:40.590 --> 00:35:44.100
And third, we know it's
not just about tools.

00:35:44.100 --> 00:35:47.610
We provide the
advisory services you

00:35:47.610 --> 00:35:50.490
need to transform
security operations.

00:35:50.490 --> 00:35:54.390
We keep customers safe with
BeyondCorp Enterprise, which

00:35:54.390 --> 00:35:58.260
enables zero trust access
for all your users.

00:35:58.260 --> 00:36:01.320
Today, we're
expanding BeyondCorp

00:36:01.320 --> 00:36:06.660
to all your applications, modern
and legacy, web and desktop,

00:36:06.660 --> 00:36:09.550
and even to production
environments.

00:36:09.550 --> 00:36:13.950
We keep customers safe by
eliminating software supply

00:36:13.950 --> 00:36:16.220
chain vulnerabilities.

00:36:16.220 --> 00:36:20.180
Over the past two decades,
we pioneered an approach

00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:23.420
to secure our own
software supply chain.

00:36:23.420 --> 00:36:25.400
We are now making
that technology

00:36:25.400 --> 00:36:30.440
available through the SLSA open
source framework and as managed

00:36:30.440 --> 00:36:35.300
services in our Cloud to help
you secure your own software

00:36:35.300 --> 00:36:36.710
supply chain.

00:36:36.710 --> 00:36:40.100
We keep customers safe by
integrating Chronicle's threat

00:36:40.100 --> 00:36:44.070
detection capability with
our Security Command Center,

00:36:44.070 --> 00:36:48.260
allowing you to respond
faster to potential risks.

00:36:48.260 --> 00:36:53.660
And we keep customers safe by
bringing our security expertise

00:36:53.660 --> 00:36:58.670
to you with our Google
Cybersecurity Action Team,

00:36:58.670 --> 00:37:01.580
a team of our leading
security experts

00:37:01.580 --> 00:37:05.330
who can help shape your
security transformation

00:37:05.330 --> 00:37:08.180
from your very
first implementation

00:37:08.180 --> 00:37:11.270
through responding
to a major incident

00:37:11.270 --> 00:37:16.260
and engineering new
solutions as needs change.

00:37:16.260 --> 00:37:20.240
Finally, we continue to
expand our security ecosystem

00:37:20.240 --> 00:37:24.380
with companies, like Fortinet,
Palo Alto Networks, Tellus,

00:37:24.380 --> 00:37:26.480
and so many more.

00:37:26.480 --> 00:37:29.180
Today, I'd like to
welcome your new security

00:37:29.180 --> 00:37:33.620
partner, Cybereason, with
whom we are collaborating

00:37:33.620 --> 00:37:37.220
to deliver a new extended
detection and response

00:37:37.220 --> 00:37:38.120
offering.

00:37:38.120 --> 00:37:41.150
That will combine
Chronicle's capability

00:37:41.150 --> 00:37:46.340
with Cybereasons mal ops engine
for faster, easier threat

00:37:46.340 --> 00:37:49.650
detection and response.

00:37:49.650 --> 00:37:53.610
Our products, our new
Cybersecurity Action Team,

00:37:53.610 --> 00:37:57.600
and our partnerships
all make the world safer

00:37:57.600 --> 00:37:59.700
from cyber threats.

00:37:59.700 --> 00:38:04.260
To talk more about how we help
keep each and every one of you

00:38:04.260 --> 00:38:07.560
secure and how we're
addressing some

00:38:07.560 --> 00:38:10.560
of the most important
challenges facing our world,

00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:12.990
I'd like to invite Sundar back.

00:38:12.990 --> 00:38:14.736
Thank you.

00:38:14.736 --> 00:38:18.010
SUNDAR PICHAI:
Thank you, Thomas.

00:38:18.010 --> 00:38:22.960
Security is top of mind for
businesses of all sizes,

00:38:22.960 --> 00:38:25.510
as well as the public sector.

00:38:25.510 --> 00:38:29.080
And despite the progress that
has been made in cybersecurity,

00:38:29.080 --> 00:38:33.280
large scale breaches
continue to make headlines.

00:38:33.280 --> 00:38:35.620
That's why, in August,
Google announced

00:38:35.620 --> 00:38:39.100
we will invest $10 billion
over the next five years

00:38:39.100 --> 00:38:41.470
to strengthen cybersecurity.

00:38:41.470 --> 00:38:44.410
That includes expanding
zero trust programs,

00:38:44.410 --> 00:38:47.110
helping secure the
software supply chain,

00:38:47.110 --> 00:38:50.440
and enhancing
open-source security.

00:38:50.440 --> 00:38:52.780
A new challenge is
keeping collaboration

00:38:52.780 --> 00:38:57.640
secure and private as we move
to hybrid work environments.

00:38:57.640 --> 00:39:02.350
To help, We are introducing
a new work safer program.

00:39:02.350 --> 00:39:06.460
It provides the highest level
of security for your email,

00:39:06.460 --> 00:39:10.690
meetings, messaging, and
more, and brings together

00:39:10.690 --> 00:39:14.830
Google Workspace with Titan
Security Keys, BeyondCorp,

00:39:14.830 --> 00:39:19.240
and other secure technologies,
products, and partners.

00:39:19.240 --> 00:39:21.970
Now, every kind of
organization in business

00:39:21.970 --> 00:39:24.670
can access the same
security protections

00:39:24.670 --> 00:39:28.410
that make work safer at Google.

00:39:28.410 --> 00:39:31.280
Security is an issue
that affects us all,

00:39:31.280 --> 00:39:35.420
and this brings us to the
last question Thomas posed.

00:39:35.420 --> 00:39:37.940
Are we addressing the
most important challenges

00:39:37.940 --> 00:39:39.960
facing our world?

00:39:39.960 --> 00:39:42.680
Climate change is one of
the most profound challenges

00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:44.120
we face.

00:39:44.120 --> 00:39:47.990
It'll take all of us working
together to solve it.

00:39:47.990 --> 00:39:50.780
Sustainability has been
a core value for us

00:39:50.780 --> 00:39:53.210
for more than two decades.

00:39:53.210 --> 00:39:56.390
Google has been carbon
neutral since 2007,

00:39:56.390 --> 00:40:00.380
and we've matched our operations
with 100% renewable energy

00:40:00.380 --> 00:40:02.870
over four consecutive years.

00:40:02.870 --> 00:40:06.320
Last year, we set out to make
our third decade of climate

00:40:06.320 --> 00:40:08.930
action our biggest yet.

00:40:08.930 --> 00:40:12.800
That Included a bold commitment
to operate on 24/7 carbon

00:40:12.800 --> 00:40:18.330
free energy across our offices
and data centers by 2030.

00:40:18.330 --> 00:40:20.640
And last week, we
announced new ways

00:40:20.640 --> 00:40:22.320
we are helping
one billion people

00:40:22.320 --> 00:40:25.450
make more sustainable choices.

00:40:25.450 --> 00:40:27.220
When it comes to
enterprises, one

00:40:27.220 --> 00:40:29.590
of the most important
sustainability choices

00:40:29.590 --> 00:40:32.290
is where to run your technology.

00:40:32.290 --> 00:40:36.730
IDC predicts Cloud migrations
over the next four years

00:40:36.730 --> 00:40:41.230
could reduce carbon emissions
by over one billion metric tons

00:40:41.230 --> 00:40:44.680
or the equivalent of
removing 200 million cars

00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:47.220
off the road for a year.

00:40:47.220 --> 00:40:50.120
We are proud that Google
Cloud is the cleanest Cloud

00:40:50.120 --> 00:40:51.840
in the industry.

00:40:51.840 --> 00:40:55.080
Earlier this year, we
introduced a way for customers

00:40:55.080 --> 00:40:59.190
to choose the cleanest regions
to run their workloads.

00:40:59.190 --> 00:41:01.500
Today, we are
expanding our portfolio

00:41:01.500 --> 00:41:05.160
of solutions and partnerships
to help reduce your carbon

00:41:05.160 --> 00:41:06.420
footprint.

00:41:06.420 --> 00:41:09.810
First, we have focused on
giving you greater transparency

00:41:09.810 --> 00:41:11.880
around carbon emissions data.

00:41:11.880 --> 00:41:15.240
We are announcing Carbon
Footprint, a new service

00:41:15.240 --> 00:41:18.630
to measure, track, and
report the gross carbon

00:41:18.630 --> 00:41:22.200
emissions associated with
your Google Cloud usage.

00:41:22.200 --> 00:41:26.050
Having this data at your
fingertips is really important,

00:41:26.050 --> 00:41:29.070
and we know that many
customers track sustainability

00:41:29.070 --> 00:41:31.360
data in other places.

00:41:31.360 --> 00:41:34.650
That's why I'm happy to announce
that Google Cloud emission

00:41:34.650 --> 00:41:39.210
data will integrate directly
into Salesforce sustainability

00:41:39.210 --> 00:41:40.450
Cloud.

00:41:40.450 --> 00:41:44.000
We also want to give you the
tools to act on the data.

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:46.810
So today, we are
introducing a new tool

00:41:46.810 --> 00:41:49.660
that will alert you when
you have idle workloads

00:41:49.660 --> 00:41:53.380
and make recommendations
to reduce carbon emissions.

00:41:53.380 --> 00:41:55.270
It's all part of
our goal to help

00:41:55.270 --> 00:41:58.930
make your Cloud transformation
secure, and sustainable,

00:41:58.930 --> 00:42:01.280
and solve for what's next.

00:42:01.280 --> 00:42:03.850
So on behalf of
Thomas and myself,

00:42:03.850 --> 00:42:06.370
let me thank you, once
again, for trusting

00:42:06.370 --> 00:42:09.890
us to be a partner with
you on this journey.

00:42:09.890 --> 00:42:13.390
And we hope you enjoy
the next three days.

00:42:13.390 --> 00:42:14.080
Thank you.

00:42:14.580 --> 00:42:17.730
[MUSIC PLAYING]

